// A mandatory machine may be replaced by another instance between two states, which may start
// again in a: the pending transition of the old instance lapses with it. So the first assertion
// holds, and the second has a counterexample from scope 2 on.

go ?
xor sm
  initial a
    [ go --> b ]
  b
  c

assert [ all m : sm | m.a && go => X (m.b || no (m ** sm)) ]
assert [ sm.a && go => X sm.b ]
